    "created_at": "2017-06-12T19:41:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-06-12T19:41:37Z",
    "body": "I believe the intent is that this path should trigger whenever any change that changes the value returned by `.textContent` occurs.  That includes textContent sets, `nodeValue` mutations on child textnodes, appends/removes of child textnodes.\r\n\r\nCertainly that's what Gecko implements: any appends/removes/mutations of textnodes directly under the textarea cause the defaultValue to change.  The \"directly\" bit I just filed as https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2752\r\n\r\nAnyway, I agree that the comefrom aspect here is unfortunate.  I'm not sure whether it's best to define this as hooks in DOM or as a mutation observer or something; unfortunately the two are observably different (in the mutation observer approach I'm quite sure we can get to a state where the textarea's kids have changed from a microtask but its value has not updated yet).",
